WEBVTT

00:00:03.168 --> 00:00:04.471
Floyd.

00:00:04.606 --> 00:00:06.273
So you came here
to get the band back together

00:00:06.409 --> 00:00:07.802
and sing
the perfect family harmony.

00:00:07.938 --> 00:00:09.542
- Yeah.
- Oh, yeah, so we can attempt

00:00:09.677 --> 00:00:11.279
to sing something
we've only tried once

00:00:11.415 --> 00:00:13.280
and failed so miserably at
that we broke up

00:00:13.416 --> 00:00:15.214
and never talked
to each other again.

00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:17.118
- We are so in!
- What?

00:00:17.253 --> 00:00:20.621
Uh, could you give us a second?

00:00:20.757 --> 00:00:21.450
Huh?

00:00:21.585 --> 00:00:23.756
Okay, what are you doing?

00:00:23.892 --> 00:00:26.194
This is your second chance
with your brothers, Branch.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.122
(sighs)
It's not that easy, okay?

00:00:28.258 --> 00:00:30.766
You don't get it.
You don't have any siblings.

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:32.160
That's my point.

00:00:32.295 --> 00:00:34.599
Branch, you are so lucky
to have a brother to fight for.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.669
I mean, if I had a sister...
(gasps)

00:00:36.805 --> 00:00:38.607
it would be so perfect.
We'd be best friends,

00:00:38.743 --> 00:00:40.410
and we'd teach each other
things, and we'd never fight.

00:00:40.545 --> 00:00:41.738
Poppy. -And we'd always
have each other's back,

00:00:41.873 --> 00:00:43.645
and we wouldn't even
have to talk

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:45.615
'cause we'd think
all the same thoughts. -Poppy.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.383
And everyone would ask us if
we were twins, and we'd laugh,

00:00:47.519 --> 00:00:48.078
and we'd be like,
"Well, not technically." -Poppy!

00:00:48.213 --> 00:00:49.149
But...

00:00:49.284 --> 00:00:50.616
if she were ever in trouble,

00:00:50.751 --> 00:00:53.249
I would do everything I could
to help her.

00:00:53.384 --> 00:00:54.549
I would show up.

00:00:54.684 --> 00:00:56.755
(sighs) Okay, listen.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.655
If there was a brother
that I might do this for--

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:02.061
and I'm not saying there is--

00:01:02.196 --> 00:01:03.624
it would be Floyd.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.001
I'm not hearing "no."

00:01:05.136 --> 00:01:06.828
- Yes! Works for me.
- Yeah!

00:01:06.964 --> 00:01:08.597
- BroZone 2.0. BroZone reunion.
- (sighs)

00:01:08.732 --> 00:01:10.064
BroZone, here we bro again.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.770
- BroZone, where'd they bro?
- (rumbling)

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:13.108
I don't know.
We're gonna find them!

00:01:13.243 --> 00:01:14.140
(spectators gasping, murmuring)

00:01:14.276 --> 00:01:15.308
- Whoa!
- (whimpers)

00:01:15.443 --> 00:01:18.009
Hey, looks like our ride's here.

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:19.379
Whoo!

00:01:19.515 --> 00:01:20.749
- Here she is.
- (panting rapidly)

00:01:20.884 --> 00:01:22.981
(chuckles)

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:24.485
(panting)

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:26.785
Oh, that's coming out
of the deposit.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.185
Meet Rhonda, y'all.
Ain't she a beaut?

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:32.228
(roaring)

00:01:32.364 --> 00:01:34.897
- She's, uh, really something.
- Oh.

00:01:35.032 --> 00:01:36.458
Um, I guess she likes me?

00:01:36.593 --> 00:01:38.100
Yeah, she does.

00:01:38.235 --> 00:01:40.136
Or she's marking you as prey.

00:01:40.272 --> 00:01:41.800
Can never quite tell
with Rhonda.

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.237
- (John Dory laughs)
- (Poppy chuckles nervously)

00:01:43.372 --> 00:01:45.636
Uh, guys, if you don't mind,

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:48.175
I really cannot wait
another minute

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:50.543
to marry this gorgeous specimen.

00:01:50.678 --> 00:01:53.848
(clears throat)
I now pronounce you

00:01:53.984 --> 00:01:55.346
husband and wife.

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:56.914
(Bridget and Gristle yell)

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.016
- (spectators cheering)
- (Bridget smooching loudly)

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:00.686
Oh!

00:02:02.085 --> 00:02:04.387
Okay, all aboard
who's going aboard.

00:02:04.522 --> 00:02:05.823
Bye, everybody!

00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:07.360
We're getting the band
back together.

00:02:07.495 --> 00:02:08.764
- Bye, Poppy.
- Bye-bye, now.

00:02:08.899 --> 00:02:09.866
Bye, Poppy.

00:02:10.001 --> 00:02:11.593
Have fun, you crazy kids.

00:02:11.729 --> 00:02:13.131
Have an awesome honeymoon!

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:14.401
Thanks, Poppy.

00:02:14.537 --> 00:02:15.971
- I love you guys!
- Peace out, Poppy.

00:02:16.106 --> 00:02:17.465
See you later, Poppy.

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:20.204
(Rhonda roars)

00:02:20.339 --> 00:02:21.507
(Rhonda beeping)

00:02:21.643 --> 00:02:23.413
KID RITZ:
Today, on a very special episode

00:02:23.548 --> 00:02:25.446
of <i>The Bop on Top,</i>
we're talking about

00:02:25.582 --> 00:02:27.814
overnight superstars
Velvet and Veneer.

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:30.480
♪ Never gets old
no matter how much I'm told ♪

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:32.516
♪ I'm amazing ♪

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.716
♪ You're amazing ♪

00:02:34.852 --> 00:02:36.519
♪ You gotta work hard ♪

00:02:36.655 --> 00:02:38.720
♪ To make it look easy ♪

00:02:38.856 --> 00:02:40.294
♪ You gotta live fast ♪

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.595
♪ To keep making that money ♪

00:02:42.731 --> 00:02:46.336
♪ If you want to be
as famous as me ♪

00:02:46.471 --> 00:02:51.039
♪ You gotta work,
gotta work, gotta work ♪

00:02:51.175 --> 00:02:52.574
♪ Watch me work. ♪

00:02:52.709 --> 00:02:54.374
So, what do you want to know?
I'm an open book.

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:56.809
Wide open. We're gaping novels.

00:02:56.944 --> 00:02:59.614
Okay, well, who are
some of your biggest influences?

00:02:59.749 --> 00:03:03.382
Honestly, Vel's always been
my inspiration.

00:03:03.517 --> 00:03:05.253
My biggest inspiration? Hmm.

00:03:05.388 --> 00:03:07.488
I'd have to go with also me.

00:03:07.624 --> 00:03:09.051
KID RITZ:
Well, one thing's for sure,

00:03:09.187 --> 00:03:11.361
after two months on the scene,
the superstar duo

00:03:11.496 --> 00:03:13.563
will receive the prestigious
Lifer Award.

00:03:13.698 --> 00:03:15.926
That's celebrating
a lifetime of achievements.

00:03:16.061 --> 00:03:18.097
Be sure to catch
their performance this weekend

00:03:18.233 --> 00:03:19.994
at the Rage Dome.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:22.000
Last question:
How do you guys stay

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:25.306
the biggest superstars
Mount Rageous has ever known?

00:03:25.442 --> 00:03:27.037
- What's your secret?
- Secret?

00:03:27.172 --> 00:03:28.742
(chuckles nervously)
We don't have a secret.

00:03:28.877 --> 00:03:30.204
(hyperventilating):
Who said we have a secret?

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:32.543
What my calm,
casual-sounding brother means

00:03:32.678 --> 00:03:34.277
is it's simple, really.

00:03:34.413 --> 00:03:38.987
It just takes lots of hard work
and loads of natural talent.

00:03:39.123 --> 00:03:41.523
(off-key vocalizing)

00:03:42.558 --> 00:03:44.055
- (Veneer whimpers)
- (Velvet groans)

00:03:44.191 --> 00:03:46.162
If we're gonna make it
through the Rage Dome show,

00:03:46.297 --> 00:03:47.788
we're gonna need more troll.

00:03:47.924 --> 00:03:49.692
Crimp, what are you doing?

00:03:49.827 --> 00:03:51.626
Why are you always hovering?

00:03:51.761 --> 00:03:53.801
Uh, I'm standing.

00:03:53.937 --> 00:03:56.804
Well, be a good little assistant
and go stand in the corner.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:57.972
Oh, yes.

00:03:58.108 --> 00:03:59.408
Um, oh, dear.

00:03:59.543 --> 00:04:02.406
I think this is
kind of a c-corner.

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:04.412
Okay, I cannot with her.

00:04:04.548 --> 00:04:05.981
- It's really too much.
- Whew.

00:04:06.117 --> 00:04:07.681
Well, time for a spritz.

00:04:07.816 --> 00:04:10.619
No, please. I barely have
any talent left to give.

00:04:10.754 --> 00:04:12.853
I mean, maybe, like,
a desperate Christmas album

00:04:12.989 --> 00:04:16.753
or a one-off national anthem
performance, but that is it.

00:04:16.888 --> 00:04:18.159
Oh, really? You don't wanna?

00:04:18.295 --> 00:04:19.561
Okay, that's fine.

00:04:19.696 --> 00:04:21.058
We'll just kiss
our careers goodbye

00:04:21.193 --> 00:04:23.194
and focus our efforts
on charity. -(chuckles)

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:25.127
Good one.

00:04:26.938 --> 00:04:28.999
(groaning)

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:33.905
(vocalizing)

00:04:36.105 --> 00:04:38.173
(sighs) That's more like it.

00:04:38.308 --> 00:04:39.912
We're so close
to having everything

00:04:40.047 --> 00:04:43.179
we always knew we believed
we deserved to have.

00:04:43.314 --> 00:04:46.081
Veneer, what's with your vibe
and your face?

00:04:46.216 --> 00:04:47.820
Why do you have
resting-moody-vibe face?

00:04:47.955 --> 00:04:49.657
No, I know
we've deserved to be famous

00:04:49.792 --> 00:04:52.193
just 'cause we want to,
but honestly,

00:04:52.328 --> 00:04:53.894
that dude looks rough.

00:04:54.029 --> 00:04:56.025
- VELVET: He's fine.
- And he's getting pale.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.164
And not in, like,
a stunning Victorian way.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:00.534
(yelps)

00:05:00.669 --> 00:05:01.999
Don't you see what you're doing?

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:04.672
You're literally sucking
the life out of me.

00:05:04.808 --> 00:05:06.102
Ugh. That's what I tell Crimp
every day.

00:05:06.237 --> 00:05:07.807
- (whimpers)
- VENEER: What are we gonna do?

00:05:07.942 --> 00:05:09.742
We obviously can't rely
on this troll

00:05:09.877 --> 00:05:11.378
to get us through
this dress rehearsal,

00:05:11.514 --> 00:05:13.012
let alone the Rage Dome show.

00:05:13.148 --> 00:05:16.614
It's all going to change
as soon as we have BroZone.

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:17.645
- BroZone?
- VELVET: Yep.

00:05:17.781 --> 00:05:19.454
I forged a letter

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:21.750
begging for them
to come and save you.

00:05:21.885 --> 00:05:23.489
(sighs):
I love me.

00:05:23.624 --> 00:05:25.560
No! You leave my brothers alone.

00:05:25.695 --> 00:05:28.463
Ugh.
I'm exhausted by this drama.

00:05:28.598 --> 00:05:30.427
Hey, do you want
to go buy a yacht?

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:31.530
Oh, good idea.

00:05:31.666 --> 00:05:33.932
Let's buy matching yachts.

